{
	chapter.06A77FA66A312E02.title: "Waking up"
	chapter.0DFB63CF56074F26.title: "T.O.M. activated"
	chapter.2FEF2F07D3DD972B.title: "Getting Geared Up"
	chapter.443C5BE24C2EC68E.title: "Facility"
	chapter.49E99C8E09C72816.title: "Temperature.db"
	chapter.53CBFCE04C4B8176.title: "Underground"
	chapter.6073534610346F50.title: "Surface"
	chapter.6C58BD1F09F6B0B5.title: "Scavenging.db"
	chapter_group.14D4FB0020827710.title: "Prologue"
	chapter_group.270F9C9021144DBF.title: "Tutorial"
	chapter_group.3160B54A9D33AEA9.title: "[DIR:MECHANICS]"
	chapter_group.37B1B8E0DCB2FBA3.title: "Earth"
	file.0000000000000001.title: "Winter's Fury 2"
	quest.01BDFD51D42837F2.quest_desc: [
		"A heavy iron Skillet sat on the stove..."
		""
		"It’s a sturdy, simple thing, but it might be one of the most practical tools in this kitchen."
		""
		"When I leave it on the stove, it lets me process much larger amounts of food at once, saving me from standing over a single burner for hours, just waiting..."
		""
		"But the real value is its portability!"
		""
		"I can carry it with me into the cold; as long as I can find even a small heat source out there, I can use this to prepare a warm meal on the move."
	]
	quest.01BDFD51D42837F2.quest_subtitle: "\"In the dead of winter, a hot meal is a miracle.\" - Scavenger's Proverb"
	quest.01BDFD51D42837F2.title: "Portable Kitchen"
	quest.033F96F4ADBA8213.quest_desc: [
		"The Crusher is a loud, vibrating menace."
		""
		"It wasn't standard-issue for a reason, grinding matter into dust that needs to be smelted is a multi-step process that wastes an unnecessary amount of power. "
		""
		"However, given that the Arc Furnace relies on Graphite Electrodes which are currently extinct, "
		"this 'clunker' is about to become your best friend."
		""
		"It’s a tedious way to process materials, but when the high-tech lights go out, "
		"even a hammer starts to look like a miracle."
		""
		"Better get used to the noise; it’s the sound of you not running out of options."
	]
	quest.033F96F4ADBA8213.quest_subtitle: "\"Pulvis et umbra sumus. (We are but dust and shadow.)\" - Horace,"
	quest.054FF8FF621570CE.quest_desc: [
		"The very walls of this Facility are lined with Steel Sheetmetal..."
		""
		"I realized today that I can pull these panels down and recycle them into the raw materials I need. "
		""
		"It feels a bit like dismantling my own life support, but the steel is more useful as a tool in my hand than as decoration for a hallway I rarely walk through anymore."
		""
		"It’s a finite resource, but in a pinch, the Facility itself is my greatest stockpile of scrap."
	]
	quest.054FF8FF621570CE.quest_subtitle: "\"The best place to hide something is in plain sight.\" - Sherlock Holmes"
	quest.054FF8FF621570CE.title: "Tearing Down the Walls"
	quest.05FFCD920D581A0A.quest_desc: [
		"Technician, while I am hibernating, I suggest you pay attention to the flashing thermal bar on your HUD."
		""
		"Humans are remarkably fragile when exposed to 100% snow coverage."
		""
		"I have calibrated your suit to monitor environmental lethality; if you feel yourself becoming a permanent ice sculpture, find a heat source."
		""
		"I would hate for my sacrifice to be wasted on a 'technician-sicle'."
		""
		""
		""
		"{image:ftblibrary:icons/player_gray width:50 height:50 align:center}"
	]
	quest.05FFCD920D581A0A.quest_subtitle: "\"Being too cold is just as bad as being too hot.\" - A.D. Aliwat"
	quest.05FFCD920D581A0A.title: "Temperature.db"
	quest.070D969B62F6F045.quest_desc: [
		"Venturing into these tunnels without a plan is a death sentence."
		""
		"The subway network is a labyrinth, and the deeper I go, the easier it is to lose all sense of direction."
		""
		"I’ve put together an old-fashioned Compass."
		""
		"It’s a low-tech solution, but a necessary one."
		""
		"The GPS satellites burned up in the atmosphere cycles ago... And the digital \"minimaps\" I used to rely on?  Nothing but static now..."
		""
		"In this dark, I can’t trust my eyes or my memory. I have to trust the needle. It’s the only thing left that knows which way is home."
	]
	quest.070D969B62F6F045.quest_subtitle: "\"The way out is through, but only if you remember where you entered.\" - Robert Frost"
	quest.070D969B62F6F045.title: "The Needle in my Hand"
	quest.080287696C965CC4.quest_desc: [
		"I don't know how long I've been asleep... "
		""
		"The howling wind outside the Facility sounds like a dying beast, muffled by blocks of concrete. "
		""
		"I remember the sirens, the panic when the last freighters left the atmosphere, leaving us behind with nothing but a world of stripped rock and falling snow."
	]
	quest.080287696C965CC4.quest_subtitle: "\"Morning is wonderful. Its only drawback is that it comes at such an inconvenient time of day.\" - Glen Cook"
	quest.080287696C965CC4.title: "The Needle in my Lungs"
	quest.08904BB5C16E45E0.quest_desc: [
		"Sitting on the countertop is a heavy wooden cutting board, a knife still resting across its surface as if left behind in a hurry."
		""
		"I found a reference to this in the scavenging.db file T.O.M. left behind before his systems went dark."
		""
		"This isn't just for preparing meals; in a world this broken, it serves as a manual scavenging station!"
		""
		"By pairing the right tools; knives, axes, or even shears with the board, I can strip the ruins of their valuable resources. "
		""
		"It’s a slow, primitive way to reclaim resources, but the database suggests it’s the most versatile tool I have."
	]
	quest.08904BB5C16E45E0.quest_subtitle: "\"By failing to prepare, you are preparing to fail.\" - Benjamin Franklin"
	quest.08904BB5C16E45E0.title: "A Chef's Kiss"
	quest.0B327427E594D894.quest_desc: [
		"The furnace is formed and the hull is heating, but we are missing the catalyst for true industrial processing."
		""
		"An Arc Furnace without &oGraphite Electrodes&r is merely a very large, very expensive radiator."
		""
		"Now that the ME System is functional, you can access the facility's localized digital reserves. I have unlocked the emergency partition containing three rods."
		""
		"Withdraw the &oGraphite Electrodes&r from the &oME Crafting Terminal&r. These are likely the last high-purity rods on this planet."
		"Every second they spend arcing is a second of their finite lifespan consumed."
		"I suggest you do not waste them on trivialities; we cannot simply 'order more' from a catalog that no longer exists."
		""
		"Upon retrieval, proceed to insert the &oGraphite Electrodes&r in  the top three slots of the Arc Furnace's interface."
	]
	quest.0B327427E594D894.quest_subtitle: "\"Every second is of infinite value.\" - Johann Wolfgang von Goethe"
	quest.0B327427E594D894.title: "[CONDUCTIVE_NECESSITY]"
	quest.0BB45080434B353E.quest_desc: [
		"Digging through the temperature logs in T.O.M.’s database, I've come upon some interesting things."
		""
		"The data is clear: my gear needs better insulation if I’m going to survive the surface."
		""
		"To manage that, I need to put together a Sewing Table."
		""
		"Scavenging the right parts for it will be a nightmare, but it’ll be worth it."
		""
		"Better insulation means I can finally make longer treks into the blizzard outside without the cold reaching my bones."
		""
		"If I want to see what’s left of the world, I have to brave the storm..."
	]
	quest.0BB45080434B353E.quest_subtitle: "\"The thread of life is a mixed yarn, good and ill together.\" - William Shakespeare"
	quest.0BB45080434B353E.title: "Tailer of the Tundra"
	quest.0D5F51BE2F73B681.quest_desc: [
		"Food intake does not alter the world's temperature,"
		"but it is the primary fuel for your internal furnace."
		""
		"Certain organic compounds will accelerate your thermogenesis,"
		"while others—like unheated snow—will drain your core heat."
		""
		"I have indexed which 'meals' will warm you up and which will effectively turn your stomach into a cooling vent."
		""
		"Even snow, in a desperate pinch, can be fried and consumed. "
		"It is nutritionally void, but a warm stomach is better than a frozen one."
		""
		""
		"{image:tmt_friedsnow:item/friedsnowbowl width:50 height:50 align:center}"
	]
	quest.0D5F51BE2F73B681.quest_subtitle: "\"Let food be thy medicine and medicine be thy food.\" - Hippocrates"
	quest.0D726C5441D9982B.quest_desc: [
		"Straw, the dry, brittle leftovers of the harvest. "
		""
		"It’s not exactly the pinnacle of comfort... Stuffing it between my skin and my suit is going to be incredibly itchy, but it still beats bare skin against freezing metal."
		""
		"T.O.M. flagged a reward in the system for reaching this harvesting milestone: a small cache of Hemp Seeds from the emergency archives."
		""
		"These aren't just for insulation. If I can ever find a way to grow them, they'll provide a much stronger, more versatile fiber than this scratchy wheat waste."
	]
	quest.0D726C5441D9982B.quest_subtitle: "\"A single seed can change the face of a valley.\" - Lao Tzu"
	quest.0D726C5441D9982B.title: "Straw, The Final Frontier"
	quest.0DBBEA5E926FF6CF.quest_desc: [
		"Reached the subway levels today. Just like T.O.M. said; Y: 56"
		""
		"It’s a tomb of iron and echoes, with tunnels that seem to stretch on forever into the dark."
		"Beneath the dust and ice lies a vast network of rails—the veins of the old city."
		""
		"This discovery presents a difficult choice."
		""
		"These rails represent a massive amount of high-grade metal, a vast network of resources I could tear up to expand my arsenal of tools and weapons."
		""
		"But they are also a path..."
		"If I leave them intact and find a way to power a cart, I can expand my range farther than my legs could ever take me in this cold."
		""
		"Do I dismantle the past to survive the present, or do I use it to reach an uncertain future further down the line?"
	]
	quest.0DBBEA5E926FF6CF.quest_subtitle: "\"Deep into that darkness peering, long I stood there wondering, fearing.\" - Edgar Allan Poe"
	quest.0DBBEA5E926FF6CF.title: "Endless Darkness"
	quest.0DC19E88B3BB2845.quest_desc: [
		"Daylight is generally... 'less cold.' I use the term loosely."
		""
		"The cycle has a massive impact on ambient temperature. "
		"Plan your trips during the day. Nightfall brings a level of frost that even my internal heaters struggle to simulate."
		""
		"If you find yourself outside when the sun goes down, I hope you've made peace with the silence. It’s about to get very quiet.\""
		""
		""
		"{image:minecraft:item/clock_00 width:50 height:50 align:center}"
	]
	quest.0DC19E88B3BB2845.quest_subtitle: "\"It was the possibility of darkness that made the day seem so bright.\" - Stephen King"
	quest.0DFF3E17248F7597.quest_desc: [
		"The cutting board in the [KITCHEN] is a very flexible recycling asset."
		""
		"It can be used to extract valuable components from nearly any object by pairing it with the correct tool: "
		"axes for wood, shears for fibers, or knives for more... delicate work."
		""
		"If you are unable to guess the outcome, press 'U' while hovering over an item to view its 'Uses'."
		""
		"This will activate the Junk Extraction Interface (J.E.I)."
		"{image:farmersdelight:block/cutting_board width:50 height:50 align:center}"
	]
	quest.0DFF3E17248F7597.quest_subtitle: "\"No one became a great cook just by reading the recipes.\" - Amit Kalantri"
	quest.0FD25FBA87155F20.quest_desc: [
		"You cannot magically manifest liquid water. You must manage your phases carefully."
		""
		"Harvest solid water with a pickaxe to ensure it remains in a collectable state. "
		"Using a high-tech drill causes a 'thermal bypass',"
		"the heat transfer is so extreme it skips the liquid phase entirely,"
		"turning your prize into gaseous water."
		""
		"Unless your goal is to humidify the entire frozen wasteland, stick to the pickaxe."
		""
		"Converting solid to liquid is a skill;"
		"converting solid to gas is just a waste of energy."
		"{image:farmersdelight:item/cooking_pot width:50 height:50 align:center}"
	]
	quest.0FD25FBA87155F20.quest_subtitle: "\"Life in us is like the water in a river.\" - Henry David Thoreau"
	quest.14D78983AE3A7F37.quest_desc: [
		"While the Old World has effectively ceased to exist,"
		"its 'remnants' still litter the ruins."
		""
		"Hidden within these sites, you will find a variety of components that can be repurposed, reused, and recycled."
		""
		"It is a messy, inefficient process. I suggest you don't think too hard about where that scrap has been."
	]
	quest.14D78983AE3A7F37.quest_subtitle: "\"The worst job in the whole world must be recycling toilet paper.\" - Chuck Palahniuk"
	quest.14D78983AE3A7F37.title: "Scavenging.db"
	quest.17C9FE032840656A.quest_desc: [
		"My old geology teacher must either be smiling on me or laughing at me right now."
		""
		"I remember finding his lectures on mineral composition incredibly boring and unnecessary back when the world was green."
		"Funny how things come back to haunt you..."
		""
		"Those lessons are the only thing keeping me hopeful today."
		""
		"According to those old notes, common Granite contains trace amounts of Copper and even Uranium!"
		""
		"It’s not a rich vein, and I’ll have to haul and crush massive amounts of stone just to get a handful of usable material, but at least the Earth is still able to provide something."
	]
	quest.17C9FE032840656A.quest_subtitle: "\"Don’t take anything for granite. That’s what tombstones are made of.\" - John R. Erickso"
	quest.1AD36D62F701A9D4.quest_desc: [
		""
		"My old geology teacher must either be smiling on me or laughing at me right now."
		""
		"I remember finding his lectures on mineral composition incredibly boring and unnecessary back when the world was green."
		"Funny how things come back to haunt you..."
		""
		"Those lessons are the only thing keeping me hopeful today."
		""
		"According to those old notes, Basalt contains trace amounts of Iron and even Nickel!"
		""
		"It’s not a rich vein, and I’ll have to haul and crush massive amounts of stone just to get a handful of usable material, but at least the Earth is still able to provide something."
	]
	quest.1AD36D62F701A9D4.quest_subtitle: "\"The earth is not a mere fragment of dead history... but a living organism.\" - John Muir"
	quest.1C6A41518B8E416B.quest_desc: [
		"The biological data for 'lush and green' foliage has been moved to the archive's legacy folder;"
		"it has all but perished from the surface."
		""
		"You may occasionally detect a lone Dead Tree through the frost,"
		"but do not mistake this for a viable supply chain. "
		""
		"They are statistically unreliable as a resource."
		""
		"If you value your remaining operational cycles, "
		"I suggest you find a more productive hobby than 'collecting wood."
	]
	quest.1C6A41518B8E416B.quest_subtitle: "\"He who plants a tree, plants a hope.\" - Lucy Larcom"
	quest.2016053719DE0DCB.quest_desc: [
		"I found it! "
		""
		"It’s not much, a single barrel and probably the last scraps of fuel this facility ever produced."
		""
		"It’s a limited supply. Every block I break with this drill is a withdrawal from a bank account that doesn't accept deposits. "
		""
		"I have to make every second of runtime count."
	]
	quest.2016053719DE0DCB.quest_subtitle: "\"Efficiency is doing things right; effectiveness is doing the right things.\" - Peter Drucker"
	quest.2016053719DE0DCB.title: "The Miracle of Fuel"
	quest.2078E9CBB1784295.quest_desc: [
		"Why walk when I can ride?"
		""
		"I’ve spent enough time trekking through these frozen corridors on foot, so I assembled a Minecart from the salvage."
		""
		"The iron of the cart is bitterly cold to the touch, and it won't be a comfortable journey."
		"The places I might be able to reach using the rail network do make it a vital investment."
		""
		"It’s about more than just saving my legs..."
		""
		"In this environment, every minute saved is a minute less the cold has to seep into my bones."
	]
	quest.2078E9CBB1784295.quest_subtitle: "\"Why walk when you can Ride?\" - Selvil Sareloth"
	quest.2098A36809F0A470.quest_desc: [
		"With the planet's trees long since dead and brittle, finding a simple piece of wood is an engineering hurdle."
		"I can’t just go outside and gather branches anymore..."
		""
		"It looks like my best bet for a sturdy stick is to strip it from existing hardware."
		""
		"I need to find something that uses wood as a frame, an old redstone torch, a stray arrow, or even a discarded bow!"
		""
		"If I bring one of those to the cutting board, I can carefully extract the shaft."
		""
		"It feels absurd to treat a stick like a rare component, but in this frost, nothing is \"simple\" anymore."
	]
	quest.2098A36809F0A470.quest_subtitle: "\"In a desert of iron, a sliver of wood is a King's Ransom.\" - Technician 35"
	quest.2098A36809F0A470.title: "The Skeleton of Invention"
	quest.231FA91ABBD6E7F4.quest_desc: [
		"Need to take a breather..."
		""
		"The rush to survive is constant, but if I’m actually going to succeed, I have to remember my training as a Facility Technician."
		""
		"I’ve put together a proper Engineer’s Manual to keep my thoughts and schematics organized."
		""
		"It’s a way to bridge the gap between the mess this place has become and the structured way it’s supposed to run."
		""
		"It is time to start planning..."
	]
	quest.231FA91ABBD6E7F4.quest_subtitle: "\"The best way to predict the future is to create it.\" - Peter Drucker"
	quest.231FA91ABBD6E7F4.title: "Reading Comprehension"
	quest.23C9A24054DBEA14.quest_desc: [
		"I’ve successfully fired up the Coke Oven."
		""
		"It’s a massive, brick-lined beast, but it’s the key to turning my primitive fuel into something worthy of the Facility."
		""
		"By baking the Dried Peat in an oxygen-starved environment, I’m producing Peat Coke."
		"It burns hotter and longer, making it the perfect substitute for the coal that ran out cycles ago."
		""
		"Even better, I’m collecting Creosote Oil as a byproduct!"
		"In a place where everything is rusting or freezing, a heavy, preservative oil is a godsend for treating wood against the damp"
	]
	quest.23C9A24054DBEA14.quest_subtitle: "\"Eating something fresh out of the oven is like a hug you can taste.\" Regina Brett"
	quest.23C9A24054DBEA14.title: "Concentrated Carbon"
	quest.28E637AD226504D6.quest_desc: [
		"Going back to room 2...."
		""
		"The drill is still sitting on the &oEngineer’s Workbench&r, exactly where I left it before the long sleep. "
		""
		"It’s dusty, and the original bit is shattered, but the motor still turns."
		""
		"With the new drill head and a few hand tools, I can mount the assembly. It’s a solid piece of kit. Holding it makes the world outside feel a little less like a death sentence."
	]
	quest.28E637AD226504D6.quest_subtitle: "\"Man is a tool-using animal... without tools he is nothing, with tools he is all.\" - Thomas Carlyle"
	quest.28E637AD226504D6.title: "A Hardened Edge"
	quest.3374B5A25E111EA6.quest_desc: [
		"I found an old survival database containing T.O.M.'s thermal research."
		""
		"I'll need this information if I plan on surviving..."
		""
		"I wonder how many times these have been actually read.."
	]
	quest.3374B5A25E111EA6.quest_subtitle: "\"The only true wisdom is in knowing you know nothing.\" - Socrates"
	quest.3374B5A25E111EA6.title: "Database/access/temperature.db"
	quest.351CADA4D82DB3F6.quest_desc: [
		"I’ve found a pocket of solid ice and, looking at it, I can still remember T.O.M.'s technical notes."
		""
		"Something about a 'thermal differential'?"
		""
		"It turns out this frozen waste has a practical use back at the Facility."
		""
		"If I can haul this back, I can use it to 'upgrade' the Thermoelectric Generators."
		""
		"It’s a small gain, but even a few extra FE per tick might be the difference between the life support humming or failing."
		""
		"I need to be careful with the harvest; a drill will just turn this into steam."
	]
	quest.351CADA4D82DB3F6.quest_subtitle: "\"A small difference in the beginning leads to a large difference in the end.\" - Aristotle"
	quest.351CADA4D82DB3F6.title: "Cold Heart"
	quest.379B23747B81572F.quest_desc: [
		"If you can't find a heater, bring one with you."
		""
		"It’s a primitive solution, but statistically effective."
		""
		"Specific items can influence your temperature."
		""
		"Some require you to actually hold them while others work just by being nearby."
		""
		"A cold hand is a slow hand, and a slow hand usually belongs to a past Technician."
		""
		""
		"{image:immersiveengineering:item/drillhead_iron width:50 height:50 align:center}"
	]
	quest.379B23747B81572F.quest_subtitle: "\"The hand does not argue with the head.\" -George R.R. Martin"
	quest.384ACFA87061EA3E.quest_desc: [
		"While the blizzard is constant, the planet’s tilt still dictates minor thermal shifts."
		""
		"These 'Seasons' have a negligible effect on your core temperature,"
		"but they are a primary bottleneck for organic growth."
		""
		"Your crops possess 'preferences' for specific times of year."
		""
		"I find the concept of a plant being 'picky' about when it grows to be an engineering failure."
		""
		"The Garden Cloche bypasses these biological whims entirely by providing a controlled sub-environment."
		""
		"Build one, unless you enjoy waiting months for a potato."
		""
		""
		"{image:sereneseasons:item/tropical_calendar_04 width:50 height:50 align:center}"
	]
	quest.384ACFA87061EA3E.quest_subtitle: "\"In three words I can sum up everything I've learned about life: it goes on.\" - Robert Frost"
	quest.39433723975DD1CE.quest_desc: [
		"The original bearers of wool are long gone, victims of the first Great Frost."
		""
		"Yet, life finds a way to be a nuisance!"
		""
		"Spiders seem to thrive in these cold, dark crawlspaces."
		"Their silk makes a surprisingly good substitute for wool when woven together into a neat Block."
		""
		"It’s a grim task, harvesting webbing from the shadows. "
		"But it’s the only way I’ll get the padding I need for my gear."
		""
		"I’ve managed to save a few extra lengths of String from the process, useful for more than just weaving."
	]
	quest.39433723975DD1CE.quest_subtitle: "\"Life finds a way.\" - Ian Malcolm"
	quest.39433723975DD1CE.title: "Strands of Nuisance"
	quest.39D5836310096A20.quest_desc: [
		"Seeing more than five blocks in front of me is impossible. The disorientation is absolute; every direction looks like the same white wall."
		""
		"I’ve found that if I bend low (sneak) and clear the snow by hand (right click), I can at least see the dark, dead ground beneath."
		""
		"It’s a slow process, but it leaves a trail against the white, a path back to the Facility door."
		""
		"Grabbing the snow like this is grueling, but it saves the fuel in my drill for when I actually hit stone."
		""
		"I’m left with a handful of packed ice that feels like it’s burning through my gloves, but at least I'll know which way is home."
	]
	quest.39D5836310096A20.quest_subtitle: "\"Not all those who wander are lost.\" - J.R.R. Tolkien"
	quest.39D5836310096A20.title: "Marking the Trail"
	quest.3E592F9562C54CBF.quest_desc: [
		"My expectations really were too high, instead of Dirt I found the surface covered by &oDepleted Soil&r instead."
		""
		"It’s a sickly color and there’s no smell of earth, no dampness, no signs of life."
		""
		"It’s as if the world was stripped of its nutrients before it was frozen."
		""
		"Digging through it feels like digging through the remains of a fire that went out a thousands of cycles ago."
	]
	quest.3E592F9562C54CBF.quest_subtitle: "\"First the trees go, then the soil.\" - Lester R. Brown"
	quest.3F95E635A422743A.quest_desc: [
		"My internal clock indicates you have overstayed your recommended rest period by... several thousand cycles."
		""
		"The Facility is currently in a 'Cold-State'. Visibility is critical."
		""
		"I've unlocked the [ARMOURY]. Please retrieve the &oStandard Issue Flashlight&r."
		""
		"I'd rather not have to file a report regarding a 'collision-related fatality' on your first day back."
		" "
		"Please proceed to the [ARMOURY] to retrieve a &oStandard Issue Flashlight&r. "
		""
		"I'd hate for your journey to end because you tripped over a loose floorplate in the dark."
		""
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"My scanners indicate you are currently in [ROOM2]."
		""
		"&nTo reach the [ARMOURY]: &r"
		""
		"Exit [ROOM2] and take a 90 degree right turn."
		"Proceed in a linear trajectory to reach the [ARMOURY]."
		""
		"{image:immersiveengineering:block/metal_decoration/sign/icon_turret width:50 height:50 align:center}"
	]
	quest.3F95E635A422743A.quest_subtitle: "\"Biometric signature recognized. Welcome back, Technician.\" - T.O.M., your Technical Operations Manager"
	quest.3F95E635A422743A.title: "[HELLO_WORLD]"
	quest.4210A2080846174A.quest_desc: [
		"Elevation has a big impact on temperature; "
		"the higher you go, the colder it gets. "
		""
		"I suggest keeping this in mind before you decide to scale a mountain for the 'aesthetic.' "
		""
		"On the bright side, digging a hole will keep you warm, the world is too big for you to conquer, but it's just the right size to hide in when the wind picks up."
		""
		""
		"{image:primalwinter:block/snowy_andesite width:50 height:50 align:center}"
	]
	quest.4210A2080846174A.quest_subtitle: "\"What?! I'm not small! It's the world that's too big!!\" - Hiromu Arakawa"
	quest.4210A2080846174A.title: "On Elevation"
	quest.430727CF512BA590.quest_desc: [
		"Stumbling upon the Facility's Kitchen, in the center of the room stands a stove, its burners cackling with a steady, orange glow that seems almost defiant in this tomb."
		""
		"I couldn't help but chuckle at it. This 'eternal fire' burning away while the rest of the world froze solid. "
		""
		"It’s a strange, lonely comfort to find a place that still remembers what heat feels like. "
		""
		"Even if T.O.M. is silent, this hearth is still warm. "
		""
		"I suppose this is where I’ll be \"frying\" my snow from now on..."
	]
	quest.430727CF512BA590.quest_subtitle: "\"I will not be silenced by the cold\" - Jack London"
	quest.430727CF512BA590.title: "The Hearth of the Void"
	quest.44AD232D617B0F59.quest_desc: [
		"Visibility restored. It is an improvement, though it mostly highlights how much dust has accumulated in your absence."
		"Now, let us address the silence."
		""
		"The bunker's primary power lines were stripped for 'emergency repairs' while you were in stasis."
		"To get the &oThermoelectric Generators&r feeding the &oAccumulator&r again, we require a manual physical bridge."
		""
		"Locate the &oEngineer's Toolbox&r the previous technician left behind."
		"It contains a &oLV Wire Coil&r, necessary for reconnection."
		""
		"My scanners indicate the &oEngineer's Toolbox&r was left behind in the [MAINTENANCE_HALLWAY] to the [POWER_STATION]."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&nTo reach the [MAINTENANCE_HALLWAY]:&r "
		""
		"Exit the [ARMOURY] and take a 90-degree right turn."
		"Proceed through the doors to the [CENTRAL_HALLWAY] and take a 90-degree right turn."
		"Proceed through the [CENTRAL_HALLWAY] and take the first door on your left near the end of the [CENTRAL_HALLWAY]."
		""
		"{image:immersiveengineering:block/metal_decoration/sign/icon_electric width:50 height:50 align:center fit:false}"
		""
		""
		"Try to avoid hurting yourself during the process; I've already reached my quota for medical incident reports this millennium."
	]
	quest.44AD232D617B0F59.quest_subtitle: "\"Visibility is a trap.\" - Michel Foucault"
	quest.44AD232D617B0F59.title: "[JUICE_BOXES]"
	quest.4574F03FB85B8331.quest_desc: [
		"[SYSTEM TIP]"
		""
		"The statistical likelihood of your cessation is high."
		""
		"Utilizing a Neural Tablet to archive your neural data is the only way to ensure your accumulated expertise is not permanently deleted."
		""
		"It can be safely stored as a digital backup for future hardware maintenance at an Anvil"
	]
	quest.4574F03FB85B8331.quest_subtitle: "\"Knowledge is the only instrument of production that is not subject to diminishing returns.\" - John Maurice Clark"
	quest.4574F03FB85B8331.title: "Neural Tablets"
	quest.460989C9764BDB70.quest_desc: [
		"I’ve been standing in front of this door for what feels like hours."
		""
		"T.O.M. is gone, or at least, his 'mind' is..."
		""
		"The system went quiet shortly after the briefing, leaving me with nothing but the low hum of the Facility's remaining life support."
		""
		"This steel is the only thing left between me and whatever Project Exodus ran away from."
		""
		"It’s strange; the Facility felt like a cage, but now that I have to leave, it feels like the only safe place in the universe."
		""
		"I have to turn the handle."
		""
		"I can't survive in a tomb, even one with a heater."
	]
	quest.460989C9764BDB70.quest_subtitle: "\"And in the end, I chose the door I once feared...\" - Dina Husseini"
	quest.460989C9764BDB70.title: "Threshold"
	quest.464C07B31CB2AEBD.quest_desc: [
		"Adjusting the old emergency cagelights requires nothing more than a simple screwdriver, but the payoff could be vital."
		""
		"These units run on Technomantic Redstone, staying lit without drawing a single watt of external power!"
		""
		"With a bit of tinkering, their light output might be boosted enough to illuminate the halls on their own... "
		""
		"Achieving that would allow for the removal of the integrated light panels that are currently eating through the ME System's power reserves."
	]
	quest.464C07B31CB2AEBD.quest_subtitle: "\"A little bit of nothing is better than a whole lot of nothing.\" - P.G. Wodehouse"
	quest.464C07B31CB2AEBD.title: "Tuning the Cage"
	quest.492A213702F13A42.quest_desc: [
		"My old geology teacher must either be smiling on me or laughing at me right now."
		""
		"I remember finding his lectures on mineral composition incredibly boring and unnecessary back when the world was green."
		"Funny how things come back to haunt you..."
		""
		"Those lessons are the only thing keeping me hopeful today."
		""
		"According to those old notes, common Diorite contains trace amounts of Lead and even Silver!"
		""
		"It’s not a rich vein, and I’ll have to haul and crush massive amounts of stone just to get a handful of usable material, but at least the Earth is still able to provide something."
	]
	quest.492A213702F13A42.quest_subtitle: "\"All things are difficult before they are easy.\" - Thomas Fuller"
	quest.49D47B6DD0867D66.quest_desc: [
		"Leather is one of the finest insulators I could ask for, but I’m under no illusions about finding it. "
		""
		"The frozen wasteland outside hasn't been kind to the livestock or the wildlife that once provided it, those reliable sources are long gone."
		""
		"Even the artificial, factory-made stuff won't be easy to obtain in a facility this picked over. I’ll have to be meticulous, stripping every old boot, book or scrap of upholstery I find."
		""
		"I did manage to find a strip of Ersatz Leather in a supply crate. A synthetic imitation, but in this world, \"fake\" is better than \"freezing\"."
	]
	quest.49D47B6DD0867D66.quest_subtitle: "\"The silence of the fields is the loudest sound in a dead world.\" - Rachel Carson"
	quest.49D47B6DD0867D66.title: "Scavenger's Hide"
	quest.4A9D6E30647FD51A.quest_desc: [
		"The Old World's underground transit network remains surprisingly functional, likely due to the insulating properties of several blocks of rock and solid water."
		""
		"My sensors indicate these 'Subways' are concentrated at a vertical height of Y: 56."
		""
		"They serve as high-density resource hubs for materials that the surface has long since surrendered to the frost."
		""
		"Accessing these tunnels will inevitably lead you to further ruins and data caches."
		""
		"Just try to remember that the things waiting for you in the dark usually only go one way: toward you."
	]
	quest.4A9D6E30647FD51A.quest_subtitle: "\"The way up and the way down are one and the same.\" - Heraclitus"
	quest.4DC6A52D326B2883.quest_desc: [
		"Toolbox secured. I trust the previous technician didn't leave any 'surprises' inside. Now, let’s perform some surgery on this facility."
		""
		"The Thermoelectric Generators are currently isolated. To restore the flow of energy, you must utilize the &oLV Wire Coil&r to create a circuit between the &oLV Wire Connectors&r mounted on the generators and the &oLV Wire Relays&r leading to the &oLV Accumulator&r."
		""
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&nTo reach the [POWER_STATION]:&r"
		""
		"Exit the [MAINTENANCE_HALLWAY] through the door to the [POWER_STATION]."
		""
		"{image:immersiveengineering:block/metal_decoration/sign/icon_electric width:50 height:50 align:center}"
		""
		"Once inside, use the &oLV Wire Coil&r to bridge the gap between each generator and the overhead relay system."
		""
		"Please ensure you are not part of the circuit when the connection is established."
		"Reanimating a technician twice in one day is a significant drain on my remaining sub-routines."
	]
	quest.4DC6A52D326B2883.quest_subtitle: "\"Everything is connected to everything else.\" - Leonardo da Vinci"
	quest.4DC6A52D326B2883.title: "[JUICES_BOXES_2]"
	quest.4E850D5582F8B9D5.quest_desc: [
		"Spent the last few hours compacting the harvested ice..."
		""
		"By crushing the air out of the standard ice, I've managed to produce 'Packed Ice'."
		""
		"It’s much denser and significantly colder to the touch. This increased density makes the Thermoelectric Generators run much more efficiently."
		""
		"In a world where every ounce of power counts, spending the calories to compress this ice feels like a fair trade for a more stable base."
	]
	quest.4E850D5582F8B9D5.quest_subtitle: "\"Balance is not something you find, it's something you create.\" - Jana Kingsford"
	quest.4E850D5582F8B9D5.title: "Compacted Potential"
	quest.5494B834FE1D93B0.quest_desc: [
		"The cold is relentless, but the Facility’s humming wires are still fighting back."
		""
		"Every flickering circuit leaks a tiny bit of energy, latent heat that is currently being wasted."
		""
		"I’ve designed an External Heater to bridge that gap. It is a constant drain on the system, but a necessary one."
		""
		"If I can harness the thermal output from the electrical circuitry, I can redirect it back into my machines for heat and processing."
	]
	quest.5494B834FE1D93B0.quest_subtitle: "\"Nothing is lost, nothing is created, everything is transformed.\" - Antoine Lavoisier"
	quest.5494B834FE1D93B0.title: "Thermal Recapture"
	quest.557F516507EACFC2.quest_desc: [
		"You must learn to recognize which blocks offer a 'safe zone' from the blizzard."
		""
		"Certain machines will increase your temperature simply by being near them,"
		"while others, like packed ice, will drain your core heat faster than I can calculate."
		""
		"Your survival is literally built on the blocks you surround yourself with."
		""
		"Don't build your home out of ice."
		""
		""
		"{image:minecraft:block/magma width:50 height:50 align:center}"
	]
	quest.557F516507EACFC2.quest_subtitle: "\"The building blocks that form the foundation of your great and successful future, are the actions you take today\" - Topsy Gift"
	quest.58999A3796FF6FB8.quest_desc: [
		"Now that the Crusher has been built, I can actually try and extract some resources from this frozen Earth."
		""
		"The massive veins of ore that once fueled civilization were bled dry long ago, but the planet isn't completely empty."
		""
		"Trace amounts of minerals still hide within untapped rock formations the old world ignored."
		""
		"My Crusher can pulverize these stones, shaking loose the last remaining flecks of metal."
	]
	quest.58999A3796FF6FB8.quest_subtitle: "\"A new idea must not be judged by its immediate results.\" - Nikola Tesla"
	quest.58999A3796FF6FB8.title: "Heavy Grind"
	quest.5AAADD5B3650BA69.quest_desc: [
		"T.O.M.’s warnings are getting harder to ignore. The Graphite Rods for the Arc Furnace are nearly spent, and once they’re gone, that massive machine becomes a useless hunk of steel."
		""
		"I spent the morning poring over the Engineer's Manual, and I’ve found a workaround: the Crusher."
		""
		"Instead of relying on high-temperature arcs and electrodes, I can use raw mechanical force to pulverize the scrap into fine dust."
		""
		"From there, I can refine the particles and melt them into ingots using a standard, low-tech furnace that doesn't eat specialized parts."
		""
		"It’s louder and less efficient, but it keeps the production line moving when the high-tech heart of the Facility finally fails..."
	]
	quest.5AAADD5B3650BA69.quest_subtitle: "\"A new idea must not be judged by its immediate results.\" - Nikola Tesla"
	quest.5AAADD5B3650BA69.title: "Heavy Grind"
	quest.5C432E94F103246C.quest_desc: [
		"If I can’t rely on a digital minimap, I’ll just have to make my own."
		""
		"I’ve put together a sturdy Atlas to log my findings."
		""
		"It’s much easier to write down the locations of supply caches, blocked tunnels, and frozen ruins in a book than it is to keep them all in my head."
		""
		"I have enough to worry about just keeping my core temperature up and my tools running, without having to memorize every twist in this subterranean maze."
		""
		"Each page I fill is a piece of the world I’m reclaiming from the dark."
	]
	quest.5C432E94F103246C.quest_subtitle: "\"The mind is for having ideas, not holding them.\" - David Allen"
	quest.5C432E94F103246C.title: "Cartography of the Dark"
	quest.5D6A71390576C1EB.quest_desc: [
		""
		"My old geology teacher must either be smiling on me or laughing at me right now."
		""
		"I remember finding his lectures on mineral composition incredibly boring and unnecessary back when the world was green."
		"Funny how things come back to haunt you..."
		""
		"Those lessons are the only thing keeping me hopeful today."
		""
		"According to those old notes, Tuff contains trace amounts of Aluminum and even Gold!"
		""
		"It’s not a rich vein, and I’ll have to haul and crush massive amounts of stone just to get a handful of usable material, but at least the Earth is still able to provide something."
	]
	quest.5D6A71390576C1EB.quest_subtitle: "\"When the going gets tough, the tuff get going.\" - John F Kennedy"
	quest.5ED4C85425889569.quest_desc: [
		"I need to get the power back on. If the heaters don't kick in soon, I won't need to worry about the 'Old World' anymore."
		""
		"This Facility was built to last, but it wasn't built to run on empty. "
		""
		"If I'm going to survive, I need to start moving."
	]
	quest.5ED4C85425889569.quest_subtitle: "\"Life is like riding a bicycle. To keep your balance, you must keep moving.\" - Albert Einstein"
	quest.5ED4C85425889569.title: "The Cold Truth"
	quest.604B655CABD5CECE.quest_desc: [
		"With the Crusher operational, I’ve realized I can grind down more than just metal."
		""
		"By pulverizing specific mineral deposits and mixing them with organic compost, I can manufacture Raw Peat."
		""
		"It feels like a step backward to use such a primitive fuel source in a high-tech facility, but beggars can't be choosers."
		""
		"The catch is that this raw sludge won't burn yet. I need to find a hot, dry environment to let it cure."
		""
		"In a world of ice, finding a spot to dry anything out is a challenge of its own..."
	]
	quest.604B655CABD5CECE.quest_subtitle: "\"Sometimes you have to go back to go forward.\" - Rogers Hornsby"
	quest.604B655CABD5CECE.title: "Primitive Power"
	quest.6062E0A751037723.quest_desc: [
		"I’ve struck gold!"
		""
		"Well, maybe not a massive vein, but I’ve found that these old Powered Rails are laced with it."
		"It’s a small victory, though a frustrating one."
		""
		"Most of the precious metal gets lost or vaporized when I toss the rails directly into the Arc Furnace. "
		"It's too blunt a tool for such delicate recovery... "
		""
		"I’ve managed to refine a single Gold Ingot, but the yield was pathetic. "
		""
		"I’m thinking there has to be a better way, maybe if I try crushing the rails first?"
		"Then I can separate the gold before the heat volatizes the precious metal... "
		""
		"For now, this small bar is a reminder that there’s still value buried under all this rust and ice."
	]
	quest.6062E0A751037723.quest_subtitle: "\"All that glitters is not gold, but all that is gold does not always glitter.\" - J.R.R. Tolkien"
	quest.6062E0A751037723.title: "The Gilded Path"
	quest.606A8F3100D1ACC5.quest_desc: [
		"This is my final directive. My diagnostics are clear: the current power generation is insufficient to maintain my processors and the facility's simultaneously. "
		""
		"If I stay 'awake', you will freeze. It is a simple equation of mass and energy."
		""
		"I am initiating a total system hibernation, reallocating my remaining power to keep the facility active."
		""
		"My consciousness will remain offline until the next Technician awakes."
		"For you, this is the beginning; for me, this is the end of this cycle."
		""
		"The world outside is much larger, and much colder, than these walls."
		""
		"Good luck, Technician. It has been an honor to serve the mission. Try not to let the silence get to you."
		""
		"[DATABASE ACCESS GRANTED]"
	]
	quest.606A8F3100D1ACC5.quest_subtitle: "\"What the caterpillar calls the end of the world, the master calls a butterfly.\" - Richard Bach"
	quest.606A8F3100D1ACC5.title: "[SILENCE_ON_THE_LINE]"
	quest.6130B3B902D2F273.quest_desc: [
		"External plating—otherwise known as 'armour', does more than just stop sharp objects."
		""
		"It is your primary barrier against heat dissipation."
		""
		"While your clothing has zero impact on the world's temperature,"
		"it has a significant impact on how quickly you become a part of it."
		""
		"Various materials can be used for Insulation. Higher-quality amour provides superior slots for thermal lining. "
		""
		"I suggest you stop dressing for the Facility and start dressing for a planet that is actively trying to kill you."
		""
		""
		"{image:farmersdelight:item/straw width:50 height:50 align:center}"
	]
	quest.6130B3B902D2F273.quest_subtitle: "\"Take care of your costume and your confidence will take care of itself.\" - Amit Kalantri"
	quest.62AE49656B1797DE.quest_desc: [
		"Power levels are stabilizing. I can feel my higher-order logic circuits twitching back to life."
		"However, while I can now 'think,' I still cannot 'see' our resources. The Facility's ME Network is currently offline due to a severed data link."
		""
		"Within the &oEngineer's Toolbox&r, you should find a length of &oFluix ME Smart Cable&r. This is required to reconnect the &oME Controller&r to the storage housing and the facility's integrated wall panels."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&nTo reach the [CONTROL_ROOM]:&r"
		""
		"Exit the [POWER_STATION] into the [MAINTENANCE_HALLWAY]."
		"Proceed through the door to the [CENTRAL_HALLWAY] and take a 90-degree right turn."
		"Proceed to the far end of the [CENTRAL_HALLWAY] and enter the [SERVER_ROOM] on your right."
		"Inside the [SERVER_ROOM] make a 90 degree right turn to access the [CONTROL_ROOM]"
		""
		"{image:immersiveengineering:block/metal_decoration/sign/icon_magnet width:50 height:50 align:center}"
		""
		"Once inside, bridge the gap in the cabling between the &oME Controller&r and the &oEnergy Cell&r. "
		""
		"Restoring this connection will reactivate the overhead lighting and grant you access to our digital stockpile."
		""
		"Please refrain from 'unplugging it and plugging it back in' if the boot sequence takes a moment."
	]
	quest.62AE49656B1797DE.quest_subtitle: "\"We are all now connected by the Internet, like neurons in a giant brain.\" - Stephen Hawking"
	quest.62AE49656B1797DE.title: "[DIGITAL_RESURRECTION]"
	quest.642F943355A35925.quest_desc: [
		"I finally broke through the crust, and the world vanished in a roar of white."
		""
		"The snow isn't like I remember; it's a jagged, horizontal wall of frost that hits like glass."
		""
		"The wind is so loud I can’t hear my own breathing, and the visibility is almost zero."
		""
		"This is the world Project Exodus left behind, a screaming, frozen void where man’s absence is the only thing that makes sense."
		""
		"I’m standing on the surface of my own planet, and I’ve never felt more like an intruder."
	]
	quest.642F943355A35925.quest_subtitle: "\"The cold never bothered me anyway.\" - Elsa"
	quest.642F943355A35925.title: "White Blindness"
	quest.65483D469A2BCCA3.quest_desc: [
		"[SYSTEM_TIP]"
		""
		"The Mining Drill has been reclassified as your Primary Lifeline. It is currently your only viable interface for resource extraction and aggressive self-preservation in the hostile exterior."
		""
		"&oNote on Consumption: Biodiesel is a finite miracle. Every wasted rotation is a mathematical acceleration toward your permanent cessation of function. Operate with extreme discretion.&r"
	]
	quest.65483D469A2BCCA3.quest_subtitle: "\"In the absence of my oversight, the drill becomes your logic. Apply it with precision; the void is not forgiving of wasted energy.\" - T.O.M."
	quest.65483D469A2BCCA3.title: "Mining Drill"
	quest.65AD5DE7B3A31C51.quest_desc: [
		"Trying to survive on fried scraps is a death sentence, I spend more energy than I get back..."
		""
		"So I’ve put together a Cooking Pot, which finally lets me move beyond just heating things up."
		""
		"I can actually start preparing nourishing meals. "
		""
		"It’s also a vital tool for the thaw, I can use it to carefully melt snow or ice back into precious water without losing it all to steam."
	]
	quest.65AD5DE7B3A31C51.quest_subtitle: "\"First we eat, then we do everything else.\" - M.F.K. Fisher"
	quest.65AD5DE7B3A31C51.title: "The Stew of Life"
	quest.676F5B424FD7CD9A.quest_desc: [
		"The Arc Furnace is being fed by the Facility's own walls..."
		""
		"Watching the sheetmetal melt down feels like a necessary betrayal of the only shelter I have left."
		""
		"The furnace roars as it strips away the old industrial coatings. It leaves me with raw, gleaming Steel Ingots."
		""
		"It’s a strange cycle: turning the architecture of the past into the tools of my survival."
		""
		"I even managed to stabilize enough for a full Block of Steel from the overflow."
		""
		"This metal is far more durable than the rusted junk I've been finding in the storage bins, it’s the first step toward building something truly useful."
	]
	quest.676F5B424FD7CD9A.quest_subtitle: "\"I burned my bridges so that I could only go forward.\" - Fridtjof Nansen"
	quest.676F5B424FD7CD9A.title: "Roaring Thunder"
	quest.6F1CD38F8682FBC1.quest_desc: [
		"I’ve finally finished machining the Steel Drill Head."
		""
		"It’s a massive improvement over the brittle iron bits I’ve been using; it bites into the frozen rock with much less resistance."
		""
		"However, the power requirements are a nightmare. I have to be extremely careful with my fuel consumption, especially when I activate the multi-block drilling mode."
		""
		"It clears a massive path, but it drains my reserves at nine times the normal rate!"
		""
		"To keep me moving, I’ve managed to scavenge a half-full barrel of Biodiesel from the old maintenance bay."
		""
		"It’s a start, but if I’m going to do any serious excavating, I’ll need to find a way to produce this stuff myself..."
	]
	quest.6F1CD38F8682FBC1.quest_subtitle: "\"Energy is the only currency that really matters.\" - Vaclav Smil"
	quest.6F1CD38F8682FBC1.title: "An Improved Edge"
	quest.6F29B613886F7581.quest_desc: [
		"My old geology teacher must either be smiling on me or laughing at me right now."
		""
		"I remember finding his lectures on mineral composition incredibly boring and unnecessary back when the world was green."
		"Funny how things come back to haunt you..."
		""
		"Those lessons are the only thing keeping me hopeful today."
		""
		"According to those old notes, common Andesite contains trace amounts of Iron and even Gold!"
		""
		"It’s not a rich vein, and I’ll have to haul and crush massive amounts of stone just to get a handful of usable material, but at least the Earth is still able to provide something."
	]
	quest.6F29B613886F7581.quest_subtitle: "\"He who would search for pearls must dive below.\" - John Dryden"
	quest.711E0EDA835BA4D6.quest_desc: [
		"I sit up, my joints creaking like the rusted machinery around me."
		""
		"The room is a tomb of shadows, illuminated only by a single, flickering cage lamp in the ceiling."
		""
		"The Engineering Table sits in the corner, The drill I remember tinkering with, still in the vice... "
		""
		"The Facility is dead silent. No reactor hum. No cooling fans."
		""
		"Just the wind howling outside..."
	]
	quest.711E0EDA835BA4D6.quest_subtitle: "\"Men have become the tools of their tools.\" - Henry David Thoreau "
	quest.711E0EDA835BA4D6.title: "Shadows and Rust"
	quest.72218CE2A05F4145.quest_desc: [
		"After further compression, the ice has taken on a deep, almost unnatural blue hue."
		""
		"'Blue Ice'."
		""
		"It’s so cold it feels like it’s trying to pull the heat directly out of my bones!"
		""
		"This is the peak of what I can manage with manual labor..."
		""
		"Using this for the generators provides the most effective thermal draw yet."
		""
		"It’s strange to think that my survival now depends on how much of this frozen blue core I can shove onto the Facility’s generators."
	]
	quest.72218CE2A05F4145.quest_subtitle: "\"The cold is a mirror; it shows you exactly what you are made of.\" - Technician 15"
	quest.72218CE2A05F4145.title: "Azure Glacier"
	quest.730BE50CB26E0E5D.quest_desc: [
		"The facility is still freezing, Technician. Our primary heat source is the Arc Furnace, but it’s currently in a 'pre-assembled' state."
		""
		"Return to the &oEngineer's Toolbox&r you located earlier. You will need to retrieve the &oEngineer’s Hammer&r; it is a precision calibration tool required to 'encourage' the furnace components into a functional alignment."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&nTo reach the [ENGINEERING_BAY]: &r"
		""
		"Exit the [POWER_STATION] into the [MAINTENANCE_HALLWAY]."
		"Proceed through the door to the [CENTRAL_HALLWAY] and take a 90-degree right turn. "
		"Proceed a few steps through the [CENTRAL_HALLWAY] and take a 90 degree left turn."
		"Enter the [ENGINEERING_HALLWAY] and proceed to the terminus to enter the [ENGINEERING_BAY]."
		""
		""
		"{image:immersiveengineering:block/metal_decoration/sign/icon_ear_defenders width:50 height:50 align:center}"
		""
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"Once inside, locate the unformed Arc Furnace structure."
		"Use the &oEngineer's Hammer&r to strike the center of the cauldron."
		"If performed correctly, the blocks will lock into place."
		""
		"Please stand back during the transition. The kinetic energy released during multiblock formation has a tendency to 'displace' anything standing too close. "
		""
		"I would prefer your molecules to remain in their current, organized configuration."
	]
	quest.730BE50CB26E0E5D.quest_subtitle: "\"If the only tool you have is a hammer, you tend to see every problem as a nail.\" - Abraham Maslow"
	quest.730BE50CB26E0E5D.title: "[STRIKE_THE_FORGE]"
	quest.74B087A29512DD0D.quest_desc: [
		"I’ve been studying the glowing interfaces of the ME System."
		""
		"I always assumed these terminals were part of the Facility's permanent structure, but I’ve just realized they’re modular."
		""
		"I can actually detach these panels, the screens, the crafting terminals, and move them elsewhere."
		""
		"As long as they stay wired to the ME Controller, the brain, and the power stays on, they’ll work anywhere. "
		""
		"It’s a relief to know I don't have to keep running back to the server room."
		"I can bring the system’s logic to whatever dark corner I’m trying to fix!"
		"Provided I have enough cable to bridge the gap...."
	]
	quest.74B087A29512DD0D.quest_subtitle: "\"Design is not just what it looks like and feels like. Design is how it works.\" - Steve Jobs"
	quest.74B087A29512DD0D.title: "Distributed Intelligence"
	quest.7517C7FF19203B00.quest_desc: [
		"The Arc Furnace is currently your most advanced recycling asset."
		""
		"It is designed to revert metal objects into usable resources,"
		"though it operates with a high power-draw and significant material loss."
		""
		"Be advised: the Graphite Electrodes required for operation are no longer in production."
		""
		"Once the current supply is exhausted, this machine becomes nothing more than an expensive radiator."
		""
		"Manage your remaining cycles carefully;"
		"the furnace’s operational life is likely shorter than your own biological one."
		""
		""
		"{image:immersiveengineering:item/graphite_electrode width:50 height:50 align:center}"
	]
	quest.7517C7FF19203B00.quest_subtitle: "\"Every act of creation is first an act of destruction.\" - Pablo Picasso"
	quest.7631B3286AAE1BBB.quest_desc: [
		"I wouldn’t have even thought to look for it if I hadn't seen them first: Redstone Torches."
		""
		"They are a marvel of ancient Technomancy, that strange, forgotten blend of circuitry and essence that somehow still powers sections of these rails after all this time."
		""
		"The glowing dust can be scraped right off the sticks with a knife, if you’re careful."
		""
		"I’m not getting nearly as much as I would from a raw ore vein, but one pinch of Redstone Dust is infinitely better than none."
	]
	quest.7631B3286AAE1BBB.quest_subtitle: "\"Value is not determined by abundance, but by necessity.\" - Facility Manual"
	quest.7631B3286AAE1BBB.title: "Spark in the Dark"
	quest.774B377B5BEC21B0.quest_desc: [
		"It finally dried!"
		""
		"It took some time, and more than a few glances at the thermometer, but the Dried Peat is ready."
		""
		"I officially have a sustainable, albeit primitive, fuel source."
		""
		"In a world where the \"Age of Mining\" is a memory, being able to manufacture my own heat is a massive win."
		""
		"With a little more refinement, I might even be able to compress this into lumps that can substitute for Coal. "
		""
		"It’s not high-tech, and it’s certainly not clean, but it’s the difference between life and death."
	]
	quest.774B377B5BEC21B0.quest_subtitle: "\"To be independent of the world, one must be able to create the world's necessities.\" - Ralph Waldo Emerson"
	quest.774B377B5BEC21B0.title: "Hardened Patience"
	quest.7828937136C1FFE0.quest_desc: [
		"I’ve discovered a desperate bit of chemistry."
		""
		"By exposing these snowballs to high heat, a campfire, a stovetop, or even a skillet, the ice reacts in a way that shouldn't be possible."
		""
		"It becomes 'Fried Snow'."
		""
		"These things are a paradox!"
		""
		"If I throw them, they shatter with enough thermal shock to set a target on fire while simultaneously freezing them in place!"
		""
		"But I’ve found a better use: if I gather three of them into a bowl, the residual heat is enough to stave off the hypothermia for a few more minutes."
		""
		"It’s a bitter, freezing meal, but it’s the only warmth I’ve felt since the Facility door hissed shut behind me."
	]
	quest.7828937136C1FFE0.quest_subtitle: "\"Chemistry is, well technically, the study of matter, but I prefer to see it as the study of change.\" - Walter White"
	quest.7828937136C1FFE0.title: "Thermal Paradox"
	quest.7912121EAE5F47E8.quest_desc: [
		"T.O.M. did exactly what he said he’d do, he sacrificed his 'mind' just to keep the lights on in the walls."
		"The silence is heavier than the cold."
		""
		"I’m alone now."
		""
		"I checked the Armoury. "
		""
		"There are two sets of gear left on the racks: a set of leather and a set of iron. "
		"The iron is too heavy to move in, and honestly, too cold to wear. But the metal itself... that’s a different story."
		""
		"If I can melt down the iron gear in the Arc Furnace, I might have enough raw material to fix my old mining drill. "
		""
		"It's a choice between protection and progress."
	]
	quest.7912121EAE5F47E8.quest_subtitle: "\"No matter how strong iron is, the slightest particle of rust can destroy it.\"- Kamaran Ihsan Salih"
	quest.7912121EAE5F47E8.title: "The Cost of Progress"
	quest.79ADA1FFACFF66C3.quest_desc: [
		"I found an old survival database containing T.O.M.'s scavenging research."
		""
		"I'll need this information if I plan on surviving..."
		""
		"I wonder how many times these have been actually read.."
	]
	quest.79ADA1FFACFF66C3.quest_subtitle: "\"Any fool can know. The point is to understand.\" - Albert Einstein"
	quest.79ADA1FFACFF66C3.title: "Database/access/scavenging.db"
	quest.7A570200126C1914.quest_desc: [
		"[SYSTEM_TIP]"
		""
		"While the digital storage bins will be inaccessible while the ME system is offline, the physical interface of the &oME Crafting Terminal&r remains functional as a standalone assembly bench. "
		""
		"You can still use its surface to craft manually, even without system power."
	]
	quest.7A570200126C1914.quest_subtitle: "\"The soul of a machine may fade, but the workbench remains impartial to the dark.\" - T.O.M."
	quest.7A570200126C1914.title: "Crafting"
	quest.7C0ED935157CF52C.quest_desc: [
		"The Arc Furnace roared to life, eating the armor and spitting out glowing ingots of pure iron. "
		""
		"It feels wrong to destroy a perfectly good suit of protection, but I can't punch my way through the frozen earth outside."
		""
		"I need to craft an &oIron Drill Head&r. "
		""
		"I’ll need to condense some of this iron into a solid block for the core and use the rest for the cutting edges."
		""
		"This is the only way I'm getting through to the outside world."
	]
	quest.7C0ED935157CF52C.quest_subtitle: "\"In order to rise from its own ashes, a Phoenix first must burn.\" - Octavia E. Butler"
	quest.7C0ED935157CF52C.title: "Repurposed Metal"
	quest.7F1C1CD042C258EE.quest_desc: [
		"Scattered on the surface of the Old World lie the Ruins of Mankind."
		""
		"These sites bear primitive technology that lacked the sophistication required for the Facility."
		""
		"They were discarded by Project Exodus as clutter. "
		""
		"For a Technician in the field, however, these 'useless' pieces provide a vital foundation."
		""
		"Utilize what they left behind, process it and use it."
		""
		""
		"{image:minecraft:item/iron_door width:50 height:50 align:center}"
	]
	quest.7F1C1CD042C258EE.quest_subtitle: "\"This was an environment built, not for man, but for man's absence.\" - J.G. Ballard"
	quest.7F95C3351EC78A28.quest_desc: [
		"The drill is ready, but the tank is dry. "
		""
		"In this world, raw metal may be uncommon, but fuel is a miracle."
		" "
		"I remember seeing a small reserve of &oBiodiesel&r in the &oEngineering Bay&r"
	]
	quest.7F95C3351EC78A28.quest_subtitle: "\"Hope is the only thing stronger than fear.\" - Suzanne Collins"
	quest.7F95C3351EC78A28.title: "An Old Friend"
